**List Reports** is for the moment you need the raw rows, not a chart: every student who was absent
yesterday, every duplicate RFID, every unpaid fee. It sits at the top level of the side drawer,
under **Help & What's New**.

Lists are **read-only**. Nothing you do here changes a record. Access is granted by the *List
reports (view & download raw data)* key in **Administration → Access Control**, and lists that
contain money also need the matching accounting permission. If a list isn't offered to you, you will
not see it in the catalogue.

## Finding a list

The catalogue groups lists under **Students**, **Teachers & staff**, **Attendance**, **Exams**,
**Accounting**, **Admissions** and **School structure**. The header shows how many you can see
(*12 of 40 lists*). Type in **Search lists** (for example "RFID", "absent" or "teachers") to narrow
it. *No lists match your search.* means nothing matches; *No lists are available to this account.*
means your access doesn't include any.

Some lists you may be looking for:

- **Students** — All students, students with a missing or invalid contact number, students sharing a
  contact number, students without a valid class, duplicate RFIDs and student IDs, birthdays and
  ages, left students, deleted students, student achievements, certificates issued, class lists.
- **Attendance** — students absent on a date, students present or late on a date, attendance % for a
  period, day-by-day student register, daily attendance by class, teachers absent or present on a
  date, teacher timesheet, declared teacher absences, and the raw tap log.
- **Exams** — exams, exam results, marks below the pass mark, missing marks, exam summary per
  student, term report remarks and conduct, and the mark change log.
- **Accounting** — fee charges, outstanding fees, fee balance per student, discounts, ledger,
  payments, refunds and voids, day closes, the online payment inbox, fee types and schedules, and
  teacher salaries.
- **Admissions** — admission applications and admission fee payments.

## Working with a list

Open a list. If it needs a date, class or exam, set the filters at the top and press **Show**
(*Set the filters and press Show.*). **Reset** clears them. Then:

- **Search these rows** matches text in any column.
- **Columns** chooses which columns to show.
- Click a header to sort; numbers sort numerically and blanks go last.
- Filter dropdowns appear for columns with a small set of values.

A very long list is cut off: a red note says *Showing the first N of M rows. Narrow the filters to
see the rest.* Narrow the filters rather than expecting the download to contain the missing rows.

## Download

Use the export menu to download as **CSV** or **PDF**. The file contains the rows currently shown
(after your search and filters) and only the columns you have left switched on under **Columns**.
The PDF is only offered when 25 or fewer columns are shown; otherwise hide some columns or use CSV.

